  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/45885A">Example <span data-tag="45885A">5.4.5.9</span>.</a> Let $\calI $ be a $\tau $-filtered $\infty $-category, and let $p: K \rightarrow \calI $ be a $\tau $-small diagram. Then the projection $\calI _{p/} \rightarrow \calI $ is $\tau $-cofinal. To prove this, consider a $\tau $-small diagram $K' \rightarrow \calI _{p/}$ where $K'$ is weakly contractible, corresponding to a map $q: K \star K' \rightarrow \calI $. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/0ED3F9" data-tag="0ED3F9">4.2.3.6</a>, the inclusion $K' \subseteq K \star K'$ is right anodyne, so that the map $\calI _{q/} \rightarrow \calI _{q|K'/}$ is a trivial fibration (and therefore weakly cofinal). </p>
